From: LFRon <ronforever@outlook.com>
Date: 2026-10-19 17:59:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: keep GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2 queryable for 1.0 instances

The Android loader resolves this entrypoint's core name through
vkGetInstanceProcAddr while initializing its driver dispatch table, for
instances of every requested apiVersion, and stores the answer without
falling back to the KHR name. Its WSI code then calls the stored pointer
without a NULL check when probing R8G8B8 surface format support.

Keep the entrypoint queryable regardless of the version the instance
requested. Filtering what applications can see is the loader's job.

Signed-off-by: LFRon <ronforever@outlook.com>
---
diff --git a/src/vulkan/util/vk_dispatch_table_gen.py b/src/vulkan/util/vk_dispatch_table_gen.py
index c2776d26..41488171 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/util/vk_dispatch_table_gen.py
+++ b/src/vulkan/util/vk_dispatch_table_gen.py
@@ -512,7 +512,9 @@ vk_physical_device_entrypoint_is_enabled(int index, uint32_t core_version,
 % for e in physical_device_entrypoints:
    case ${e.entry_table_index}:
       /* ${e.name} */
-   % if e.core_version:
+   % if e.name == 'GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2':
+      return true;
+   % elif e.core_version:
       return ${e.core_version.c_vk_version()} <= core_version;
    % elif e.extensions:
      % for ext in e.extensions:
